:: Asylum Depths Mirror 2
<<effects>>

After a moment, the mirror's surface stirs, glows, and shifts. It doesn't reflect you, or your audience, but a 
<<if C.npc.Sydney.gender is "m">>
	boy
<<else>>
	girl
<</if>>
sat alone, face in hands, tears running between <<nnpc_his "Sydney">> fingers.
<br><br>

<<person1>>

<<if C.npc.Sydney.init is 1>>
	<<nnpc_He "Sydney">> looks familiar, but the
<<else>>
	The
<</if>>
image lasts only a moment. It swirls, fades, and is replaced by the <<person>>. <<He>> now has a cocktail in one hand, and a lit cigarette in the other.
<br><br>
<<asylum_depths_mirror_links>>

<<if $tiredness gte C.tiredness.max>>
	<span class="blue">You're too tired to dance right now.</span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Dance (0:20)|Asylum Depths Mirror Dance]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<pass 20>><<tiredness 6>><<danceskill 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gdanceskill>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Leave|Asylum Depths]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Mirror 3
<<effects>>

<<generate5>><<person5>>
After a moment, the mirror's surface stirs, and glows. It spreads to the other mirrors. The glow fades, and your perspective has shifted. You squint as a bright light fills your vision.
<br><br>

Your eyes adjust. You're now looking at the stage, rather than the audience. A person stands in the middle, a light centred on their face, concealing their identity. They hold their hands in front of them in a meek posture, and to their side stands a <<person>> you don't recognise, wearing a doctor's outfit.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths Mirror 3 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Mirror 3 2
<<effects>>

"As you can see," the <<person5>><<person>> says. "Our patient is now somewhat more pliant." You hear an audience chuckle around you, amused by some in-joke. "Observe." <<He>> clicks <<his>> fingers. The mystery figure drops to their knees, and presses their forehead to the ground.
<br><br>

The image blackens, as if the lights died, then you're on stage once more. Your audience faces you, eager as ever.
<br><br>

<<person1>>
<<asylum_depths_mirror_links>>

<<if $tiredness gte C.tiredness.max>>
	<span class="blue">You're too tired to dance right now.</span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Dance (0:20)|Asylum Depths Mirror Dance]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<pass 20>><<tiredness 6>><<danceskill 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gdanceskill>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Leave|Asylum Depths]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Mirror 4
<<effects>>

The lights flicker, then die, plunging you into darkness.
<br><br>

"Sorry for the interurption folks," says a voice. "We'll have the lights on in a jiffy." Sure enough, they return in just a moment. You're stood behind the stage, peeking out from behind the curtain.
<br><br>

"You're ready for this," the <<person1>><<person>> says, resting a hand on your shoulder. "I know you won't disappoint."
<br><br>


<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths Mirror 4 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Mirror 4 2
<<effects>>

The <<person>> steps by you, out onto the stage. "Ladies and gentlemen," <<he>> says. "It's time for the main event. You probably know <<phim>> as <<overworld_nickname>>. The more daring of you might know <<phim>> as <<underworld_nickname>>. Regardless, please join me in a round of applause for the greatest sensation this town has ever produced."
<br><br>

The <<person>> bows out of your way as you step onto the stage. The applause is defeaning.
<br><br>

<<link [[Tell a joke|Asylum Depths Mirror 4 Joke]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Dance|Asylum Depths Mirror 4 Dance]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[This isn't real|Asylum Depths Mirror 4 Willpower]]>><</link>>
<br>

