<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Office 1 Clear
<<effects>>

You examine the furniture, not wanting to disturb the chaos without knowing how everything is supported.
<br><br>
<<if $housekeepingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_office to 2>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_small_carried += 1>>
	There's a pile of notes you think you can move without issue. They look like inventory paperwork, mostly. You move them aside in batches, <span class="green">clearing the way into the office proper.</span>
	<br><br>

	It looks like it used be a private office, but other furniture has since been dumped here. You see a glint in the corner of your eye. <span class="gold">A small mirror stands half concealed beneath a sheet.</span> You free it from its hiding place. 
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You think you've figured it out, but when you try to move a single dusty notebook, <span class="red"> the stacked desks beside it tremble.</span> You flee the room, but there's no avalanche.<<ghousekeeping>><<housekeeping 1>>
	<br><br>

	You leave the room as messy as ever.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Office 2 Clear
<<effects>>

Many chairs have been stacked in front of the windows. 
<<if $housekeepingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_office to 3>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_medium_carried += 1>>
	They're a little stuck, but you pry the topmost free with stationary, and lower it to the ground. There's space in other rooms. <span class="green">You manage to move them all,</span> letting in natural light.
	<br><br>

	<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
	You open a window to let in a fresh breeze. It blows some papers aside, revealing a familiar face. A younger Doctor Harper stares up at you, face blank, nothing but a white wall behind <<him>>. The photo is loose, and none of the documents nearby mention <<him>>.
	<br><br>
	You find a medium-sized mirror while searching, half-hidden behind one of the remaining chairs.	
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>><br><br>

	You return to the hallways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>

<<else>>
