<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Office 3 Clear
<<effects>>

Several desks are crammed together, taking up most of the room.
<<if $housekeepingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_office to 4>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_large_carried += 1>>
	They're heavy, but you notice they're built from several components, attached with a simple mechanism. You take them apart, and carry the pieces to other rooms, <span class="green">clearing the space.</span>
	<br><br>
	One desk is different. Larger. It looks like an antique. A large mirror lies flat on its top.
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br> 
	You shift the mirror, and find a sheet of paper underneath.
	<br>
	<i>"Tell those upstarts I don't care what they're offering. The mirrors work, and I'm not replacing them with their jiggery-pokery."</i>
	<br><br>

	You return to the hallways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You try to move them, but they're heavy, and quite old. You hear creak, a snap, <span class="red">and a splinter assaults your face.</span> You'll have to try another time.<<gpain>><<pain 4>><<gstress>><<stress 6>><<ghousekeeping>><<housekeeping 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Office 4 Clear
<<effects>>

Paperwork litters the floor, so thick and uneven you almost trip, and all of it coated in dust.
<<if $housekeepingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_office to 5>>
	You begin the task of sorting it into the filing cabinets around the edge of the room. You work with broad strokes. Inventory manifests in one cabinet, patient records over there. <span class="green">You clean up faster than you expected.</span>
	<br><br>
	The office clean, you sit at the main desk, lean back, and admire your handiwork. Then you hear a knock at the door.
	<br><br>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	"Excuse me," says a <<personsimple>>'s voice. A <<person>> steps in, and looks around. "I had family here, and they won't let me access the records. Can I look around?"<<gggcool>><<asylumstatus 9>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Accept|Asylum Depths Office 4 Accept]]>><<trauma -6>><</link>><<ltrauma>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Refuse|Asylum Depths Office 4 Refuse]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You try to shift it into semi-tidy piles, but uneven thickness and size makes them unsteady. They soon collapse, <span class="red">undoing your work.</span> You'll have to try another time. <<ghousekeeping>><<housekeeping 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Office 4 Accept
<<effects>>

You nod.
<br><br>
"Thank you." The <<person>> steps forward, and rifles through cabinets, until <<he>> finds what <<he>>'s looking for.
<br><br>

You sit for a few more moments, then return to the hallways.
<br><br>
<<earnFeat "Record Keeper">>

