:: Asylum Depths Garden 2 Trim
<<effects>>

You approach the wall of brambles. The sound of running water is louder here. You cut the plants, aiming for the thickest, most exposed branches.
<<if $tendingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_garden to 3>>
	<<set $asylum_tunnels to 1>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_medium_carried += 1>>
	<span class="green">You're surprised by the effectiveness.</span> The smaller branches fall limp, as if in surrender.
	<br><br>
	
	You step over them, and find the source of the sound. A small river. It flows from the forest, into a tunnel running beneath the asylum.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">You've found the tunnels.</span>
	<br><br>
	You also find a door set into the wall beside the tunnel. Inside is a small room. There's a basin, towels, and a medium-sized mirror. All in good condition.
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps the mirror would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps the mirror will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	You enter the asylum once more.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You squeeze as hard as you can, <span class="red">but you're unable to do more than dent their surface.</span> Perhaps they're too blunt.<<gtending>><<tending 1>>
	<br><br>

	You enter the asylum once more.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Asylum Depths Garden 3 Trim
<<effects>>

You dig around the stumps littering the middle of the garden, and try to pull one free.
<<if $tendingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_garden to 4>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_large_carried += 1>>
	It's stuck firm, but you feel the pressure points, and dig around a little more. This time, <span class="green">you succeed.</span>
	<br><br>

	You continue pulling them, stump after stump. Then you fill in the holes with loose soil. Grass should grow here fine.
	<br><br>
	
	You turn to enter the asylum once more, and find a large mirror leaning against the door. You're not sure how it got here, but
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You tug as hard as you can, until you feel it loosen. You fall on your <<bottom>>, <span class="red">with only splinters in your hands.</span><<gpain>><<pain 4>><<gtending>><<tending 1>>
	<br><br>

	You enter the asylum once more.
	<br><br>
	
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Asylum Depths Garden 4 Trim
<<effects>>

The garden is clear, and would look inviting, if not for the barbed, vine-like branches swinging from above, threatening to cut you at the whim of the wind.
<br><br>
<<if $tendingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_garden to 5>>
	You find a branch, and intercept the branches as they cross, snagging them. Stilled, you're able to pull them further down, <span class="green">and give them a good trim.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths Garden 4 Trim 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You try to grab them as they pass, <span class="red">but get only pricked as a reward.</span> Another time.<<gpain>><<pain 4>><<gtending>><<tending 1>>
	<br><br>
	
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Asylum Depths Garden 4 Trim 2
<<effects>>
<<generateyv1>><<generate2>><<generate3>>
The last seems to shudder when you release it. It blows in the breeze, then it settles. As it does, movement catches your eye beyond it, and beyond the fence.
<br><br>
A car appears between the trees, driving along a road obscured by bushes. It comes to a stop outside another part of the asylum. A pair of figures climb out, a <<person2>><<person>> and <<person3>><<person>>, and walk towards the building.
<br><br>
Tall double doors open. Doctor Harper steps out, with a <<person1>><<person>> beside <<him>>. You recognise <<him>> as one of the asylum patients. <<He>> wears a vacant smile on <<his>> face. Harper keeps a firm grip on the <<persons>> shoulder.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths Garden 4 Trim 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Garden 4 Trim 3
<<effects>>

The <<person1>><<person>> remains silent, but the others talk. They're too far to hear, aside from one moment when a breeze delivers the <<person2>><<person>>'s shrill laugh.
<br><br>

The <<person2>><<person>> and <<person3>><<person>> take the <<person1>><<person>> by each arm, and lead <<him>> back to the car. Harper waves as they drive away.
<br><br>

You enter the asylum once more.
<br><br>
<<earnFeat "Bramble Tamer">>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Garden Trim
<<effects>>

You trim the brambles surrounding the hidden garden, keeping them at bay. You learn a thing or two.
<br><br>

Satisfied, you return to the hallways.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>



:: Asylum Depths Garden Relax
<<effects>>

You sit on the soft grass in the hidden garden,

<<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
	sheltered from the rain by the boughs above, listen to it pitter patter all around. It's peaceful.
<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
	watching the snow settle. It's peaceful. Even the sound of the sea is swallowed by the icy forest between you.
<<else>>
	watching the sky, and the subtle movements of the forest beyond the fence. It's peaceful.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Satisfied, you return to the hallways.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><</link>>


:: Asylum Depths Tunnels 1 Swim
<<effects>>

<<swim_strip>>
<<water>>
You step into the water. The current is stronger than it looks, pushing you back against the bars of the fence.
<<if $swimmingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_tunnels to 2>>
	You swim against it, <span class="green">and enter the tunnel.</span> <<physique 3>>
	<br><br>
	It's dark further inside, but you don't go far. You clamber onto the bricks, into a dry space littered with detritus. Light reflects off a small mirror.
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>> 
	<<set $asylum_mirror_small_carried += 1>>
	<br><br>
	You peer further down the tunnel. Your eyes adjust to the gloom, and you see that it branches. You'd be able to swim up there, but the current doesn't look any more gentle. 
	<br><br>
	You climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You strain against it, <span class="red">but you're unable make it to the tunnel.</span><<physique 3>><<swimmingskilluse>>
	<br><br>
	
	You climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, then enter the asylum.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>



:: Asylum Depths Tunnels 2 Swim
<<effects>>

<<swim_strip>>
<<water>>
You swim down the tunnel, into the dark, to the spot where it branches. You swim in one direction, only to find it branching again. It's a maze of tunnels. <<physique 3>>
<br><br>
<<if $swimmingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_tunnels to 3>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_medium_carried += 1>>
	<span class="green">You're able to navigate them,</span> helped by light entering through gratings above. Until you turn a corner, and see a pitch black tunnel ahead.
	<br><br>

	You feel something brush your shoulder. A medium-sized mirror floats by, buoyed by its lightweight frame.
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br> 
	You swim back to the garden, climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>
	
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You find it hard to navigate in the gloom, <span class="red">and find yourself swimming back to the garden without meaning to.</span> <<swimmingskilluse>>
	<br><br>
	
	You climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>



:: Asylum Depths Tunnels 3 Swim
<<effects>>

<<swim_strip>>
<<water>>
<<if $swimmingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_tunnels to 4>>
	<<set $asylum_mirror_large_carried += 1>>
	You navigate the deeper tunnels, feeling your way along the walls. The flow of the current helps your sense of direction, <span class="green">and you're able to make it even deeper than before.</span> <<physique 3>>
	<br><br>
	You see a space up ahead, lit by a red light. You turn the corner, and see a baleful light above a metal door. You pull yourself up.
	<br><br>
	The door has no handle, nor any way of opening it from this side, but the marks on the floor, along with footsteps in the dust, suggest occasional use. Beside it, thick with grime, stands a large mirror.
	<<if $asylum_mirror gte 2>>
		Perhaps it would be happier in the mirror room.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<<else>>
		Perhaps it will be useful later.<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	The frame is lightweight, and the water won't hurt it. Might help get it clean.
	<br><br>

	You swim back to the garden, climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You try to navigate the tunnels, <span class="red">but soon lose your direction in the dark.</span> You follow the current back to the garden.<<physique 3>><<swimmingskilluse>>
	<br><br>
	
	You climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>



:: Asylum Depths Tunnels 4 Swim
<<effects>>

<<swim_strip>>
<<water>>
You dive into the water, and swim along the tunnels, pushing against the current until you reach the submerged passage. You take a deep breath, and try to swim to the other side. <<physique 3>>
<br><br>

<<if $swimmingSuccess>>
	<<set $asylum_tunnels to 5>>
	You keep your eyes on the dim light up ahead, 
	You emerge in a large room, lit only by light seeping through grating far above. <span class="pink">You feel a presence.</span> Two yellows eyes open, and stare at you.<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
	<br><br>

	The eyes lurch closer, and you step back, but then they stop. You hear a deep breathing. Then you notice the bars, barely visible in the dark. The creature is caged.
	<br><br>

	There's a lever to the side. A mechanism links it to the cage door.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Pull the lever|Asylum Depths Tunnels 4 Pull]]>><<set $asylum_tunnels to 6>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Asylum Depths Tunnel 4 Leave]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You make it some way, but the light ahead seems to shimmer and fade. <span class="red">You feel disoriented,</span> and turn back the way you came. You gulp in the air.<<swimmingskilluse>>
	<br><br>
	
	You climb onto the shore, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Asylum Depths Tunnel 4 Leave
<<effects>>

You swim back to the garden, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
<br>

:: Asylum Depths Tunnels 4 Pull
<<effects>>

You pull the lever. With a screech of tortured metal, the cage door rises. The eyes stay still a moment, then the creature steps into the weak light. It rises, stretches, towering over you. The eyes look down at you for a moment, then it leaps into the water. There's no splash. You shiver.
<br><br>

You look around the room, but there's little else. You swim back to the garden, dry yourself, dress, and enter the asylum.
<br><br>

<<earnFeat "Eyes in the Night">>
<span class="gold">You've gained the Eyes in the Night trait.</span>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Asylum Depths]]>><<dry>><<clotheson>><</link>>
<br>

